        "content": "# Hypothesis Document: add\n**Version**: 1.0.0 | **Created**: 2026-04-03 | **Status**: PENDING\n\n## Hypotheses\n\n### HYP-001: Bun.file() API supports exists() and text() methods\n**Risk Level**: HIGH\n**Status**: PENDING\n**Statement**: The design assumes Bun.file(path) returns an object with an `exists()` method (returning a Promise<boolean>) and a `text()` method (returning a Promise<string>) for reading file contents as UTF-8.\n**Context**: The CLI entry point (src/validate-yaml.ts) depends entirely on these APIs for file existence checking and content reading. If unavailable, the implementation approach must change.\n**Validation Criteria**:\n- CONFIRM if: `Bun.file(path).exists()` returns a Promise<boolean> and `Bun.file(path).text()` returns a Promise<string> with file content\n- REJECT if: These methods do not exist or behave differently than expected\n**Suggested Method**: CODE_EXPERIMENT\n\n### HYP-002: process.argv is available and works in Bun for CLI argument parsing\n**Risk Level**: MEDIUM\n**Status**: PENDING\n**Statement**: The design assumes process.argv is available in Bun and follows the Node.js convention where argv[0] is the runtime, argv[1] is the script, and argv[2]+ are user arguments.\n**Context**: The CLI entry point uses process.argv[2] to read the file path argument. The existing src/index.ts already uses this pattern, but it should be confirmed.\n**Validation Criteria**:\n- CONFIRM if: process.argv[2] correctly receives the first user-provided argument when running `bun run src/file.ts arg`\n- REJECT if: process.argv is not available or argument positions differ\n**Suggested Method**: CODEBASE_ANALYSIS\n\n### HYP-003: process.exit() works correctly in Bun for setting exit codes\n**Risk Level**: MEDIUM\n**Status**: PENDING\n**Statement**: The design assumes process.exit(code) terminates the Bun process with the specified exit code, matching Node.js behavior.\n**Context**: REQ-005 requires exit code 0 for valid YAML and exit code 1 for errors. The implementation calls process.exit() explicitly.\n**Validation Criteria**:\n- CONFIRM if: process.exit(0) and process.exit(1) produce the correct exit codes in Bun\n- REJECT if: process.exit() is unavailable or exit codes are not propagated correctly\n**Suggested Method**: CODE_EXPERIMENT\n\n### HYP-004: Bun can run TypeScript files directly via package.json scripts\n**Risk Level**: LOW\n**Status**: PENDING\n**Statement**: The design assumes `bun run src/validate-yaml.ts` works as a package.json script entry, with Bun executing TypeScript directly without a compilation step.\n**Context**: The package.json will have a \"validate\" script set to \"bun run src/validate-yaml.ts\". The existing \"dev\" script follows this pattern.\n**Validation Criteria**:\n- CONFIRM if: Existing `bun run dev` (which runs `bun run src/index.ts`) executes TypeScript directly without errors\n- REJECT if: Bun requires a build step or cannot run .ts files directly\n**Suggested Method**: CODEBASE_ANALYSIS\n\n### HYP-005: A hand-written line-by-line YAML parser is feasible for basic syntax validation\n**Risk Level**: HIGH\n**Status**: PENDING\n**Statement**: The design proposes a line-by-line state machine parser that can validate basic YAML syntax (indentation, mappings, sequences, quoted strings, block scalars, flow collections, comments) without using any YAML parsing library.\n**Context**: This is the core technical approach for the entire feature. If a hand-written parser cannot reliably handle these YAML constructs, the implementation will be significantly more complex or may need a different approach. The no-dependency constraint (REQ-003) makes this the only viable path.\n**Validation Criteria**:\n- CONFIRM if: A state-machine approach can correctly identify valid/invalid YAML for the specified syntax subset (indentation, mappings, sequences, quoted strings, block scalars, flow collections)\n- REJECT if: The YAML syntax subset is too complex for a line-by-line approach and requires a full recursive descent parser or other fundamentally different technique\n**Suggested Method**: EXTERNAL_RESEARCH\n\n### HYP-006: Bun's test runner can discover and run co-located .test.ts files\n**Risk Level**: LOW\n**Status**: PENDING\n**Statement**: The design assumes `bun test` will automatically discover and run `src/yaml-validator.test.ts` alongside the existing `src/utils.test.ts`.\n**Context**: The testing strategy relies on Bun's test runner finding the new test file. The existing project already uses this pattern.\n**Validation Criteria**:\n- CONFIRM if: `bun test` discovers and runs all `*.test.ts` files in the src/ directory\n- REJECT if: Bun test runner requires explicit configuration to find additional test files\n**Suggested Method**: CODE_EXPERIMENT\n"
