        "content": "---\nrp1_run_id: b79a7997-5b41-45bd-8249-668945b4331b\n---\n# Development Tasks: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: add\n**Status**: Not Started\n**Progress**: 0% (0 of 8 tasks)\n**Estimated Effort**: 2 days\n**Started**: 2026-04-03\n\n## Overview\n\nA CLI command that validates YAML file syntax within the existing Bun/TypeScript project. The implementation uses a hand-written YAML syntax validator (no new dependencies) exposed through a dedicated CLI entry point, with separated pure-function validation logic, co-located tests, and a package.json script entry.\n\n## Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [T1] - Foundation module with no dependencies on other new components\n2. [T2, T3, T4] - All depend on T1's exported interface, but are independent of each other\n\n**Dependencies**:\n\n- T2 -> T1 (Interface: CLI entry point imports `validateYaml` function and types from the validator module)\n- T3 -> T1 (Interface: Tests import `validateYaml` function and `ValidationResult` type from the validator module)\n- T4 -> T2 (Build: Package script references `src/validate-yaml.ts` as the entry point)\n\n**Critical Path**: T1 -> T2 -> T4\n\n## Task Subflow\n\n```mermaid\nstateDiagram-v2\n    [*] --> T1\n    T1 : YAML Validator Module\n    T1 --> T2\n    T1 --> T3\n    T2 : CLI Entry Point\n    T3 : Validator Tests\n    T2 --> T4\n    T4 : Package Script\n    T3 --> [*]\n    T4 --> [*]\n```\n\n## Task Breakdown\n\n### Foundation\n\n- [ ] **T1**: Implement YAML validator module with line-by-line state-machine parser supporting indentation tracking, mapping/sequence syntax, quoted strings, multi-line block scalars, flow collections, comments, document markers, and special values `[complexity:complex]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#31-module-srcyaml-validatorts](design.md#31-module-srcyaml-validatorts)\n\n    **Effort**: 8 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] File `src/yaml-validator.ts` exports `ValidationResult` interface, `ValidationError` interface, and `validateYaml` function matching the public interface specification\n    - [ ] `ParserState` internal model tracks `indentStack`, `contextStack`, `inBlockScalar`, `blockScalarIndent`, `lineNumber`, and `errors`\n    - [ ] Validates indentation consistency (spaces only, no tabs; child indented further than parent; de-indent to previously established level)\n    - [ ] Validates mapping syntax (key-colon-space separator, duplicate key detection at same level)\n    - [ ] Validates sequence syntax (dash-space prefix, consistent indentation within a sequence)\n    - [ ] Validates quoted strings (matching single/double quotes, proper escape handling in double-quoted strings)\n    - [ ] Validates multi-line block scalar indicators (`|`, `>`, `|+`, `|-`, `>+`, `>-`) with content at deeper indentation\n    - [ ] Recognizes comments (full-line `#` and inline space-`#`) as valid\n    - [ ] Treats empty/whitespace-only lines as valid\n    - [ ] Validates flow collections (matching braces `{}` and brackets `[]`)\n    - [ ] Recognizes document markers (`---`, `...`) at top level\n    - [ ] Recognizes special scalar values (`null`, `true`, `false`, `~`, numeric values)\n    - [ ] Returns `{ valid: true, errors: [] }` for well-formed input and `{ valid: false, errors: [...] }` with line numbers for malformed input\n\n### Consumer Components\n\n- [ ] **T2**: Implement CLI entry point with argument parsing, file existence check, file reading via Bun.file API, validation invocation, and formatted output with exit codes `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#32-module-srcvalidate-yamlts](design.md#32-module-srcvalidate-yamlts)\n\n    **Effort**: 2 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] File `src/validate-yaml.ts` imports `validateYaml` from `./yaml-validator`\n    - [ ] Reads file path from `process.argv[2]`; prints `Usage: bun run validate <filepath>` and exits with code 1 when missing\n    - [ ] Uses `Bun.file(path).exists()` to check file existence; prints `Error: File not found: <filepath>` and exits with code 1 when not found\n    - [ ] Reads file content via `Bun.file(path).text()` as UTF-8\n    - [ ] Prints `Valid YAML: <filepath>` to stdout and exits with code 0 on success\n    - [ ] Prints `Invalid YAML: <filepath>` followed by `  Line <N>: <message>` per error to stderr and exits with code 1 on failure\n\n- [ ] **T3**: Implement test suite for yaml-validator covering valid YAML structures, invalid YAML detection, error reporting quality, and edge cases `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#7-testing-strategy](design.md#7-testing-strategy)\n\n    **Effort**: 4 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] File `src/yaml-validator.test.ts` imports `validateYaml` and `ValidationResult` from `./yaml-validator`\n    - [ ] Valid YAML cases return `{ valid: true, errors: [] }`: simple key-value, nested mappings, sequences, mixed mappings/sequences, quoted strings, multi-line block scalars, comments, empty content, document markers, flow collections, various scalar types\n    - [ ] Invalid YAML cases return `{ valid: false, errors: [...] }`: tab indentation, inconsistent indentation, missing colon-space separator, unmatched quotes, unmatched braces/brackets, invalid block scalar indentation\n    - [ ] Error objects include approximate line numbers and descriptive messages\n    - [ ] All tests pass when run with `bun test`\n\n- [ ] **T4**: Add `validate` script entry to package.json pointing to `src/validate-yaml.ts` `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#33-integration-with-packagejson](design.md#33-integration-with-packagejson)\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] `package.json` contains `\"validate\": \"bun run src/validate-yaml.ts\"` in the `scripts` section\n    - [ ] No new entries added to `dependencies` or `devDependencies`\n    - [ ] Command is invokable via `bun run 